ai-sandbox — third-party attribution
=====================================

This product bundles source code from the following third-party projects.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Termux terminal libraries  (terminal-emulator/, terminal-view/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vendored under UC-21 to render a real ANSI/VT terminal in the Android client.

  Origin:   https://github.com/termux/termux-app
            (modules `terminal-emulator` and `terminal-view`)
  Upstream lineage: derived from "Terminal Emulator for Android"
            https://github.com/jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0 — see LICENSE-termux.

Copyright (C) Termux contributors and the Terminal Emulator for Android
authors.

Modifications made in ai-sandbox (each retains the Apache-2.0 license):

  * The JNI local-process module was NOT vendored. Specifically
    `com/termux/terminal/JNI.java` and `src/main/jni/**` (the native
    `termux.c` pseudoterminal spawner) are omitted: the ai-sandbox client
    has no local shell — the shell runs in a remote Docker container and
    is reached over a WebSocket.

  * `com/termux/terminal/TerminalSession.java` was rewritten to be driven
    by that external byte stream instead of a local PTY: outbound bytes
    (keystrokes + emulator replies) are forwarded to a pluggable
    `OutputListener` (wired to the WebSocket), and inbound PTY stdout is
    pushed in via `appendToEmulator(byte[], int)`. The public API consumed
    by `TerminalView` is unchanged.

  * A `getBytesAvailable()` accessor was added to
    `com/termux/terminal/ByteQueue.java`.

  * The Groovy `build.gradle` + maven-publish config of each module was
    replaced with a Kotlin-DSL `build.gradle.kts` wired to this repo's
    Gradle version catalog. No functional code changes.

  * Upstream unit tests under `src/test/**` were not vendored.

`com/termux/view/**` is vendored unmodified.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
JetBrains Mono  (android/src/main/res/font/, android/src/main/assets/fonts/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bundled to give the terminal / tmux view (and the Compose mono chrome) a
deterministic monospace typeface with full box-drawing (U+2500–U+257F) and
block-element (U+2580–U+259F) coverage, fixing blocky glyph rendering on OEM
skins (e.g. ColorOS) whose default monospace font covers those ranges poorly.

  Origin:   https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
  Release:  v2.304 (static TTFs, from JetBrainsMono-2.304.zip)
  License:  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 — see LICENSE-jetbrains-mono
            (an in-APK copy is also shipped at
            android/src/main/assets/fonts/OFL.txt).

Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors
(https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono).

Bundled files (verbatim from the release; SHA-256):

  * android/src/main/res/font/jetbrains_mono_regular.ttf
    (JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf, W400)
    a0bf60ef0f83c5ed4d7a75d45838548b1f6873372dfac88f71804491898d138f

  * android/src/main/res/font/jetbrains_mono_medium.ttf
    (JetBrainsMono-Medium.ttf, W500)
    31c92d01a8a08528b718a43addf0ad3df0af2ca4b7b3290a452f70f358e14d3d

The fonts are bundled unmodified (only the res/font filenames were lowercased
